From 03082718e5342068d3adef01253210f332859c9e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 00:17:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 01/10] SEO: noindex every not-found page and stop sending
 unknown categories home

Unknown paths, guides and categories now show a noindexed 'Page not found'
page with links to all six category hubs, deadlines, remote, NYC and
collections. Unknown /categories/* used to redirect to the homepage (a soft
404), and the generic 404 page was indexable. Unknown collection ids are
noindexed too. Lovable hosting returns 200 for every path, so noindex is the
available substitute for a 404 status.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015eydvdzcxBPZCXsPy7MGLS
